language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Three coins: make all three coins face the same way (all heads or all tails) in exactly num_moves moves, each move flipping one coin.
given init : matrix indexed by [int(1..3)] of int(0..1)
given num_moves : int(1..3)
find steps : matrix indexed by [int(1..4), int(1..3)] of bool
such that
$ the first row of steps is the starting state: 1 means tails, 0 means heads
forAll j : int(1..3) . steps[1, j] <-> (init[j] = 1),
$ each of the first num_moves moves flips exactly one coin
forAll i : int(1..3) . i <= num_moves -> (sum j : int(1..3) . toInt(steps[i, j] != steps[i + 1, j])) = 1,
$ after the moves are done, the coins stay as they are
forAll i : int(1..3) . i > num_moves -> forAll j : int(1..3) . steps[i + 1, j] = steps[i, j],
$ at the end all three coins face the same way
forAll j : int(1..3) . steps[num_moves + 1, j] <-> steps[num_moves + 1, 1]
